7-zip can be used to produce self-extracting executables.

Just the lzma pack for 7-zip (downloadable from https://www.7-zip.org/sdk.html)
is needed, the 7-zip package itself is not necessary, though it might be useful. However, the 7zSD.sfx file which is needed insists on running with
administrator privileges, which the installer explicitly doesn't want.

This can be overcome by modifying the binary file, adding an appropriate
"manifest". A suitable one is 7zsd.manifest which can be added in Visual Studio:

"A Win32 resource must be added to your .exe. The type of the resource must be ‘RT_MANIFEST’ and the resource id must be ‘1’. An easy way to do this is with Visual Studio.NET:

    Open your exe in VS (file -> open file)
    Right click on it and select add resource
    Click ‘Import…’ from the dialog
    Select your manifest file
    In the ‘Resource Type’ field, enter ‘RT_MANIFEST’
    In the property grid, change the resource ID from ‘101’ to ‘1’.
    Save the exe.
"

Perhaps there is a way of doing this without installing the multiple
GB of Visual Studio?



